hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15640","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abi al-Haytham ibn Nasr ibn Dahr al-Aslami, from his father, he said: Maiz ibn Khalid ibn Malik, a man from us, came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and confessed against himself adultery, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to stone him. So we went out to the lava field of Banu Niyar and stoned him, and when he felt the touch of stones he panicked greatly. When we finished from him and returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we mentioned his panic to him. So he said: Why did you not leave him."
"15641","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abi al-Haytham ibn Nasr ibn Dahr al-Aslami, that his father narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying in his march to Khaybar to Amir ibn al-Akwa, and he was the uncle of Salamah ibn Amr ibn al-Akwa, and the name of al-Akwa was Sinan: Descend, O son of al-Akwa, chant for us some of your verses. He said: So he descended chanting for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: By Allah, were it not for Allah we would not be guided, nor give charity, nor pray. Indeed when a people transgress against us, if they want trial we refuse. So send down tranquility upon us, and make feet firm if we meet."
